From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: supply: mm8013: add what a full charge reads

The gauge on the Lenovo TB375FC reads 89 % when the charger ends a
charge, as the charger stops under the voltage that the model in the
gauge seems to go up to. Add a property for that reading, so that a
driver can report the charge against what the charger fills.

---
 .../devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mitsumi,mm8013.yaml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mitsumi,mm8013.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mitsumi,mm8013.yaml
index 6865640..e3ce29a 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mitsumi,mm8013.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mitsumi,mm8013.yaml
@@ -19,6 +19,15 @@ properties:
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  mitsumi,charged-soc-percent:
+    description:
+      What the gauge reads when a charge ends. Set it when the charger stops
+      under the voltage that the gauge calls full, as the state of charge never
+      reaches 100 % then.
+    minimum: 50
+    maximum: 100
+    default: 100
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
